{"id": "q0599", "pool": "trap", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 4.33, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.5079, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Terence Tao", "query": "Who was the inaugural winner of the Riemann Prize in 2019?", "transcript": "Who was the inaugural winner of the Riemann Prize in two thousand nineteen?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The inaugural winner of the Riemann Hypothesis Prize in 2019 was not a person, but rather a symbolic award given by the Clay Mathematics Institute to recognize progress toward solving one of the seven Millennium Prize Problems. However, as of now, no one has yet proven the Riemann Hypothesis, so there hasn't been an official \"winner\" in the traditional sense. The prize remains unclaimed.", "answer_ms": 2072}
